  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Indiana received $158M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 2,223 awards with an average award size of $71.1K. Obligations fell 96.8% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior-year totals of $8.5B in FY22, $6.7B in FY23, $6.3B in FY24, $8.1B in FY25, and $5B in FY26, with the current FY27 total at $158M. The FY27 to-date picture is concentrated: the largest industry by obligations is Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $62.6M. The largest single vendor so far is WELLPOINT FEDERAL SOLUTIONS, INC. at $62.6M. Readers should note that the current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date obligations rather than a full-year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2027 spending compare with prior years?",
        "body": "FY27 to date obligations are $158M compared with $5B in FY26 and higher totals in earlier years: $8.5B in FY22, $6.7B in FY23, $6.3B in FY24, and $8.1B in FY25. Obligations fell 96.8% year over year. The current FY27 figures are fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Department of Health and Human Services obligated $62.2M and Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $53.4M. WELLPOINT FEDERAL SOLUTIONS, INC. received $62.6M and ROCHE DIAGNOSTICS CORPORATION received $20.9M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry at $62.6M and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing follows at $17.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
